      "flags": {},
      "order": 19,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How to use this Krea V9 no-prompt style workflow",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Krea 2 V9 no-prompt style transfer workflow\n\nUse this when you want image 2's visual style applied to image 1 without typing a prompt.\n\nThe Load Image nodes use neutral placeholder filenames; replace them with your own content, style, and optional text/logo guard images before queueing.\n\nTested V9 setup:\n1. Put the content/subject image in Reference image 1 source.\n2. Put the style image in Reference image 2 source.\n3. Leave Final image prompt blank.\n4. Leave Written prompt strength at 0.0.\n5. Queue the workflow.\n\nGuide Card V9 1 - image 1 content:\n- Use image for: keep the same subject.\n- Strength: 0.80.\n- This anchors the main subject, clothing/object cues, pose, camera, and layout from image 1.\n\nGuide Card V9 2 - image 2 visual style:\n- Use image for: suggest the visual style.\n- Prepare image by: palette wash.\n- Color kept: 0.85.\n- Small details kept: 0.05.\n- Subject copying: avoid copying subject.\n- Final detail copying: 0.85.\n- Strength: 0.65 to 0.90 for people/content photos, or around 0.45 for product/object content.\n- This borrows broad palette, tone, finish, and atmosphere while suppressing image 2's subject identity.\n\nWhy quick style mode works here:\nThe quick suggest-the-visual-style recipe is tuned to behave like a style-only card by default: palette wash, very low detail, low shape copying, stronger global style reach, and subject-copy avoidance.\n\nStack Encoder V9:\n- Final image prompt: blank by design.\n- Written prompt strength: 0.0 is okay. the stack supplies a hidden role instruction from the connected guide cards.\n- Image detail level: medium is the starting point; use low if image 2 starts changing the subject.\n- When images guide: smart per-card timing.\n- Early-to-final handoff: 0.40.\n\nIf image 2 changes the people/subject too much:\n- Lower Reference 2 strength to 0.35 or 0.50.\n- Set Image detail level to low - loose idea (256).\n- In manual tuning, lower Shape copied before lowering Overall style reach.\n- Keep Subject copying at avoid copying subject.\n\nIf the style is too weak:\n- Raise Reference 2 strength slowly: 0.75, then 0.85, then 0.90. Quick style is capped at 0.90; use manual tuning with higher Overall style reach when you intentionally want stronger pull.\n- Keep Reference 1 around 0.80 so the content remains anchored.\n\nOptional text/logo guard:\nReference 3 starts off. Turn it on only when a reference contains words, logos, UI, labels, signs, or letter-like marks.\n\nLearn more:\n- docs/krea-v9-documentation-index.md\n- docs/nodes/kg-krea-2-image-guide-card-v9.md\n- docs/nodes/kg-krea-2-reference-stack-encoder-v9.md\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
